.TH BIGFLOATZERO 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatZero, bigFloatFromUint32, bigFloatCopy \- initialize or copy a binary big float
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "void bigFloatZero(BigFloat *" "x" ");"
.sp
.BI "void bigFloatFromUint32(BigFloat *" "x" ", uint32_t " "v" ");"
.sp
.BI "void bigFloatCopy(BigFloat *" "dst" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "src" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigFloatZero()
sets x to canonical positive zero: mantissa zero, exp zero, and sign 1.
.B bigFloatFromUint32()
sets x to v and normalizes its mantissa.
These constructors do not require an initialized destination.
.PP
.B bigFloatCopy()
copies the initialized value src to dst and clears unused destination limbs.
Self-copy is supported.  No memory allocation is needed.
To construct a negative nonzero value, initialize from its magnitude, then
set its sign field to \-1.
.SH RETURN VALUE
These functions return no value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatNormalize (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
